# Remote support log sink (BRC-CLOUD)

Devices POST session logs to BRC-CLOUD. **Do not ask the user to paste logs** when
the upload URL / bucket is known — fetch `/latest` (and the bucket index) first.

## Triage with Jev, never by hand

**Do not read uploaded logs line by line.** `npm run triage
[phone|android|desktop|<bucket>]` pulls the bucket, derives every fact in code,
then asks Jev — TypeSafe System One — for the judgments. If the verdict does not
name a fix, extend the extractor in `scripts/triage/core.mjs` (or add a
`<phase> done <N>ms` log line in the wallet so the next upload carries the
missing fact) rather than opening the log.

The extractor, the Jev questions and the Jev call live in
`scripts/triage/core.mjs` (no Node built-ins). `scripts/triage-logs.mjs` is
only the CLI: local sources, the printed report, flags. BRC-CLOUD vendors the
core (`npm run sync:triage` → `src/vendor/triageCore.mjs`, re-synced on every
deploy) for the live dashboard below.

## Live dashboard

`https://brc-cloud.bcryderman.workers.dev/logs-dashboard` — sign in as `$brandonc`
with a BRC-100 wallet identity proof from HandCash Desktop. Every upload to a
watched bucket is distilled by the same core + Jev within about a second and
pushed over a WebSocket. Allowed handles: `LOG_DASHBOARD_HANDLES` in
`BRC-CLOUD/wrangler.jsonc`. Code: `BRC-CLOUD/src/logDashboard.js` (Durable
Object `LogDashboard`), `logDashboardApp.js`.

### Reading the dashboard from Cursor

```bash
npm run triage verdicts                 # newest 10 verdicts, every watched device, plain text
npm run triage verdicts android -- --limit 3
npm run triage verdicts -- --json       # same, structured
```

This reads what the dashboard already distilled (no Jev call, no wallet
sign-in). It sends `Authorization: Bearer $LOG_DASHBOARD_READ_TOKEN`
(`HANDCASH-DESKTOP/.env`, a wrangler secret on BRC-CLOUD) to
`GET /logs-dashboard/api/verdicts?bucket=&limit=&format=text`. The token is
read-only and reaches that route alone. Full facts stay behind the wallet
sign-in, so use `npm run triage <device> -- --state` for those. Each block
gives severity, fix first + why, driver/owner, likely/unlikely flags, freezes
vs previous, workloads, the line before a freeze, repeating problems and
non-zero counters. Verdicts the dashboard has pruned stay in Workers Logs as
`event: "log-dashboard.verdict"` records (query them with the Cloudflare
observability MCP).

Code-derived facts: freezes by active wallet layer, blocked ms, **workloads**
(every `<phase> done <N>ms` / `+<N>ms` line becomes a span; share of blocked
time inside it; spans over 60s are waits — hidden WebView, storage lock — and
are reported as `waitsExcluded`, never as owners), **precedingLines** (last line before each freeze began — lines
after a freeze are just queued callbacks), **bursts**, **storage** (origin
quota refusals, largest keys, slow ops), grouped error families.

Jev's judgments: user-visible freeze, primary driver, **freeze owner** (chosen
among the workloads code actually found), storage contribution, **fix first**,
custody at risk, regression vs previous session, severity.

```bash
npm run triage android          # verdict
npm run triage android -- --state   # just the extracted facts, no model call
npm run triage android -- --json    # facts + raw answers
npm run triage desktop-local        # this Mac: renderer ring in durable-prefs.json + electron main.log, no upload needed
npm run triage -- --file saved.log  # any saved upload body
```

`desktop-local` also carries **activity** facts (stuck-row census with `item=`,
placeholder writes, sweeps survived), **ui** facts (React duplicate list keys and
the owning component) and **bridge** facts from `main.log` (per-method BRC-100
latency, error codes, renderer-not-ready). "Local desktop logs" means this
command — never open `main.log` or the ring by hand.

Never ask the model to count — counting, grouping and correlation stay in
`scripts/triage/core.mjs`. Needs `JEV_API_KEY` in `HANDCASH-DESKTOP/.env`
(the dashboard Worker has it as a secret).

When you add long-running wallet work, log `[<tag>] <phase> done <N>ms` when it
exceeds ~250ms so triage can attribute freezes to it without anyone reading.

## Endpoints

| | |
|---|---|
| Base | `https://brc-cloud.bcryderman.workers.dev` |
| Bucket index | `GET /v1/logs/<bucket>` |
| Latest upload | `GET /v1/logs/<bucket>/latest` |
| Last few | `GET /v1/logs/<bucket>/all` |

